From 829a7f8fae8cf0df5f49558832c8f5bad3c5dba9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 14:43:49 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] feat(2d): face to size from numbers on a stock-only setup

A new undoable FaceToSize command holds an optional SetStock (a box
with its top at the top Z) and a normal Face on the stock, from the top
Z down to the final Z in passes of the depth per pass. One undo takes
back the two. Z values are program Z (the active setup's WCS, else the
world origin). The command refuses by name: a final Z not below the top
Z, a depth per pass or stepover not above 0, a missing tool or one
narrower than the stepover, no stock and no size, a top Z under the
stock top, a final Z at or under the stock bottom.

The MCP tool face_to_size and a "Face to size" group on the Stock page
call the same command. The generated MCP reference and the MCP guide
name the tool.

Fixes #3196

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
